title: "Kinetopus Engine: A Parsimonious Physical-Mathematical Pipeline for Local-First Financial Time Series Forecasting using Sparse Identification of Dynamical Systems (SINDy)"
version: "1.0.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24166175"
date-released: "2026-08-23"
url: "https://github.com/JuanDie778/KineTopus-Engine"
repository-code: "https://github.com/JuanDie778/KineTopus-Engine"
license: "Apache-2.0"
keywords:
  - "quantitative-finance"
  - "scientific-machine-learning"
  - "sindy"
  - "dynamical-systems"
  - "stochastic-differential-equations"
  - "time-series-forecasting"
  - "cusum"
  - "splines"
  - "white-box"
abstract: >-
  Kinetopus Engine is a parsimonious, White-Box Scientific Machine Learning
  (SciML) framework that discovers governing continuous ordinary and stochastic
  differential equations directly from noisy financial and dynamic time series data
  using FFT-driven C² Splines, CUSUM structural regime-shift detection, and SINDy.
